 "schema": "pcc.claim/v1",
 "scope": "Odd-characteristic nonsingular S3 model; fixed declared support/weights, bounded output condition and explicit random-model distribution.",
 "statement": "Curve-first and mixed-degree selector assessment:7 generic degree-one identities and4 actual recovery declarations compile, canonical local audit363/0/0. Formal scope is actual endpoint coefficient splitting, three pivots and linear offset recovery branches for F,xF,yF. Exact norm pruning, all-degree triangular search/cost and single-irreducible-factor random-model bounds are hand analysis. They identify a generic-model yield bottleneck in the declared single-generator family, not an ECDLP lower bound or fixed-curve impossibility. Distinct-generator b-elimination is prospective, not implemented or compiled. No numerical or complete-algorithm claim."
